A||||6||GoCartGuy||Remodeling My Interior||||6||
Z||000000||GoCartGuy||03-30-2001||01:17 AM||||Ok, in the last post about fixing dash corners I said that I was redoing the interior of my 85 GT.  It had the original saddle tan interior and I found it quite dull compared to the exterior.(its bright yellow with a flame job on the custom hood)  I know there's some guys/gals who think I should stick with stock colors, but I'm a rebel, so I'm going with blue.  Anyways, this is day one and here's my progress so far.<P>Interior door panels:<BR>Pulled them off (be wary of the clips, I gotta replace a few of the now)<BR>Stripped the carpeting from both (WD-40 is a good way to loosen the adhesive from the carpets)<BR>Cleaned all the vinyl (409 followed by a brief acetone rub)<BR>Repainted using PlatiKote Vinyl Color<BR>Cleaned up the plastic around the door handle/lock assembly (409 followed by denatured alcohol, don't use acetone here, it'll eat the finish off the plastic)<BR>Primed and Painted plastic with Krylon Gloss White<P>Front and Rear Center Console<P>Removed all of it (phew that's alot of screws)<BR>Separated glove box from rear console and plastic plate from gear selector section<BR>Cleaned and reglued vinyl where it was loose (super glue is wonderful, although I did glue my thumb to my middle finger at one point)<BR>Repainted rear console, glove box face, and center vinyl ring<P>Dash:<BR>Its still in there, ran out of day light<BR>Removed entire instrument panel assembly<P>Headliner/roof:<BR>Pulled out sunroof (replacing torx screws tomorrow)<BR>Removed visors/hooks/retaining ring/latch assembly<BR>Pulled/cleaned/primed/painted dome light assembly<P>Well that's it so far got more planned for tomorrow and the rest of the weekend.<BR>Pull dash and repair/paint<BR>Repair center front console plastic piece<BR>Pull seats<BR>Pull/clean/prime/paint rest of interior trim<BR>Clean/Paint front center console<BR>Pull carpet from interior<BR>Fix carpet to door panels<BR>Pull and replace headliner<BR>Replace carpet<P>Hopefully I can have it all done and put back together by Monday.  Wish me luck and I'll keep you posted<BR><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||6
Z||000001||My7Fieros||03-30-2001||01:33 AM||||Hmmm, interesting. Im one of those "stick to stock" kinda people, but it does sound interesting. Got any pics? M7F<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero Se V6 4 spd<BR>1986 Fiero GT 5 spd<BR>1988 Fiero Formula auto<BR>2001 Mustang 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000002||GoCartGuy||03-30-2001||01:36 AM||||Pics will be here sometime.  They've been taken but need to be processed and scanned.  Also not being the most computer gifted person in the world I have no idea how to add them to a post.  Even though at this rate there will probably be 2 rolls easily.  At this rate I'll be able to strip the interior of a Fiero in less than an hour.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"<p>[This message has been edited by GoCartGuy (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||shiloh187||03-30-2001||01:38 AM||||wow, i am doing similar... i am not a stock guy and making my fiero as nice looking as possible... call me a rice boy if you will but the engine mods will come in time (they cost more)...  but i am painting all my panels red, red sifter, red shift boot, and i covered all the interior vinyl with a dark grey tweed...  it will look nice, i will get you all pics of what this amateur can do..<P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000004||GoCartGuy||03-30-2001||11:14 PM||||Day Two:<BR>Didn't get a whole lot done had alot of other stuff to do today and the hang over didn't help.  Anyways here it goes.<P>Finally removed dash<BR>Removed Seats<BR>Removed trim around doors<BR>Removed Headliner<BR>PlastiKoted the arm rests<P>Clean/Primed:<BR>Plastic around instrument console<BR>Misc. Trim bits on dash/doors<BR>Vents from rear center console<P>Tomorrow's game plan:<BR>Attach carpet to door panels<BR>Fix/clean dash<BR>Recoat Dash<BR>Paint all previously primed plastics<BR>Clean/prime/paint other plastics<BR>Install new headliner<BR>Pull and replace carpet<BR>Platic Dip the sunroof Hooks/new screws<P><BR>Again wish me luck and when its all done I'll post the pictures.  Gotta go drinkin now, its Friday night.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||GoCartGuy||04-01-2001||10:51 PM||||Ok, day three didn't get an update so I'll smash it all into day four.  I'm almost done, but as with all Fiero projects, I was expecting at least a 50% time increase.  So here is where we stand so far.<P>All plastic trim is done<BR>All extra vinyl is done<BR>Dash is fixed but awaiting a recoating (BTW anyone doing the broken corner repair with the Napa Flex Bumper Kit Let me know and I'll walk you through it)<BR>Door Panels are done<BR>Carpeting is installed on drivers side (this was a B**ch, its a little ghetto in the far corner near the accelerator, but you can't see it)<P>What to finish:<BR>Recoat dash<BR>Install headliner<BR>Dip/recrew Sunroof<BR>Carpet Passenger side<P>PUT IT ALL BACK TOGETHER.<P>Anyways, now for the bad news...had a slight problem with the camera and all previous pics were ruined...damn POS.  So any pics I get will be limited to final stage stuff.<P>Anybody got any questions interior remodeling let me know I'll help you out.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
